# FUNCTION 10/11 = DroneCAN_HARDPOINT_0/_1: FCU drives these with
# uavcan.equipment.hardpoint.Command id 0 and 1. PIN = GPIO() in hwdef.
#
# Polarity differs between the two rails and AP_Relay has no invert
# option, so the command sense differs too:
#   RELAY1 (IR_LED_EN, active high) -> command 1 = 100W IR lamp ON
#   RELAY2 (LED_EN, TPS16530 /EN)   -> command 1 = 80W lamps OFF
# Whoever drives the hardpoints from the FCU has to account for RELAY2.
RELAY1_FUNCTION 10
RELAY1_PIN 1
RELAY2_FUNCTION 11
RELAY2_PIN 2

# OUT2/OUT3 keep their RCIN2/RCIN3 defaults; OUT1/OUT4 are remapped below.
OUT_RATE 50

# FCU sprayer channels arrive as uavcan.equipment.actuator.ArrayCommand.
# AP_Periph maps actuator_id N onto function k_rcin<N> (k_rcin1 = 51), and
# the FCU sends actuator_id = SERVOn channel number. FCU SERVO9 = pump
# (k_sprayer_pump), SERVO10 = spinner (k_sprayer_spinner), so:
OUT4_FUNCTION 59 # RCIN9  -> PA11, Pump, CN11 + CN12
OUT1_FUNCTION 60 # RCIN10 -> PA8,  Nozzle, CN9 + CN10

# The command travels as UNITLESS: the FCU normalises its pulse over
# 1000..2000 and we expand it again over OUTn_MIN..OUTn_MAX about TRIM.
# The defaults (1100/1500/1900) would squash the range and, worse, leave
# ~1100us out of the pin with the pump commanded fully off.
OUT1_MIN 1000
OUT1_TRIM 1500
OUT1_MAX 2000
OUT4_MIN 1000
OUT4_TRIM 1500
OUT4_MAX 2000
